        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Feckenham, Geoffrey Chaucer, Huberd the Friar\n- Places: Westminster Abbey, Poets' Corner, City of Westminster, London, Palace of Westminster\n- Organizations: Collegiate Church of St Peter at Westminster\n- Works: The Friar's Tale, The Canterbury Tales\n- Roles: English churchman, abbot, poet\n\nFacts:\n- John Feckenham, also known as John Howman of Feckingham and later John de Feckenham or John Fecknam, lived from about 1515 to October 1584.\n- John Feckenham was an English churchman and the last abbot of Westminster.\n- Westminster Abbey is formally titled the Collegiate Church of St Peter at Westminster.\n- Westminster Abbey is a large, mainly Gothic abbey church in the City of Westminster, London, just west of the Palace of Westminster.\n- Geoffrey Chaucer was the first poet to be buried in Poets' Corner of Westminster Abbey.\n- \"The Friar's Tale\" is a story in \"The Canterbury Tales\" by Geoffrey Chaucer.\n- \"The Friar's Tale\" is told by Huberd the Friar.",
